  "language_probability": 1,
  "text": "This hydraulic lift raises a heavy car using pressure in trapped oil. A small input piston can multiply force because the lifting piston has a much larger area. The pump pushes nearly incompressible oil into the lift cylinder. Pressure spreads through the fluid and acts across the large piston. Force equals pressure times area so that piston produces a powerful upward push. As oil enters, the piston and lift arms rise together, carrying the car. A closed valve traps the oil to hold the car. Opening it allows a controlled descent. So, confined oil turns a compact pump into smooth, controlled lifting power.",
